{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"2026-09-04 recurrence during lettered-depressing-willet audit: MCP search/show/list initially succeeded, then a three-ticket show batch failed with Transport closed / nginx HTTP 502. An immediate single-call MCP retry also returned HTTP 502. The local checkout CLI remained functional and became the tracker fallback. This confirms the serving-path failure can recur during ordinary tracker reads, not only after this client starts an async gate."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788555100967917001,"uuid":"342652d6-4d67-4cbb-84c2-6ad4dbd12b65"}